# Teaching workspace (`/teach`)

When using the teach skill in this repo:

- Put **all** teaching artifacts under `teach/` (not the repo root):
  - `teach/MISSION.md`, `teach/RESOURCES.md`, `teach/NOTES.md`
  - `teach/lessons/`, `teach/reference/`, `teach/learning-records/`, `teach/assets/`
- Treat `teach/` as the teaching workspace root for relative links and new files.

## Lesson scripts must work on `file://`

Lessons are opened with `open teach/lessons/….html` (origin `null`).

- **Do not** use ES modules (`type="module"`, `import`/`export`) in lesson or `teach/assets` scripts — Chrome CORS-blocks them on `file://`.
- Use classic `<script src="../assets/….js">` and non-module inline scripts that call globals (e.g. `window.TeachQuiz`).
